-- ONE-TIME DATA RESET, not a schema migration — no ALTER TABLE, no new
-- columns. Required before deploying the /redeem single-device-binding
-- change (upload-worker.js POST /redeem).
--
-- Why: every code redeemed before this deploy has a redeemed_by fingerprint
-- generated by the OLD sessionStorage-based scheme, which resets every time
-- a browser tab/session closes. That value can never be reproduced again by
-- any real device. Once binding is live, the first legitimate guest whose
-- 20-day persisted session has expired and who revisits the original link
-- would generate a fresh (localStorage-based) fingerprint that doesn't match
-- the stale stored one — and get wrongly rejected as "a different device."
--
-- This reset "forgives" every pre-cutover claim. redeemed_at is left
-- untouched (it stays accurate history — the code really was redeemed then).
-- Binding only becomes meaningful for redemptions that happen after this
-- runs, which is correct: no redemption before this feature existed was
-- ever meant to be strictly enforced.
--
-- Apply via CF dashboard D1 console (token lacks D1 write access — confirmed
-- 2026-08-13) BEFORE deploying the worker change referencing redeemed_by for
-- binding. Order matters: this must run first, not after.
UPDATE access_codes SET redeemed_by = NULL WHERE redeemed_by IS NOT NULL;
